The decisive test is **`TestPermutationInvariance`**: it reconciles an input, then reconciles a version with replicas reordered and every suffix reversed, and asserts the marshalled `Report` is byte-identical.

`TestDelayedMembershipShrinksQuorum` exercises the membership case: the cluster expands `{A,B,C}` → joint → `{A,B,C,D,E}`; A and B replicate index 4, which was a majority of the old config but not of the new one. The reconciler correctly stops at index 3 and reports `E_UNSUPPORTED_COMMIT` instead of committing an under-replicated entry.

